  "notes": "There are 11 top tricks (2 spade tricks, the ♥A, 4 diamond tricks, and 4 club tricks). Finessing positions exist in both hearts and spades. By playing for an elimination, South may be able to make the contract even if West has the ♠Q and ♥K.\n\nSouth should win the club lead and cash 3 more rounds of that suit. The ♦A should be cashed next, followed by a second diamond to the dummy. When diamonds prove to be 3-2 the contract is certain.\n\nSouth cashes 1 more round of diamonds and leads a heart covering whatever East plays. West can win the trick cheaply, but he will be endplayed. Either a spade or a heart return will provide trick 12 for South.\n\nNotice the importance of keeping a late diamond entry to the dummy. A spade return by West at the time of the endplay will give South a third spade trick, however, the suit will be blocked. Dummy's diamond entry will allow South to untangle the spades.\n\nIf West shows out on the second round of diamonds, the endplay will still work as above. If West turns up with 4 diamonds the elimination will no longer work as removing West's exit cards in diamonds will also remove dummy's entry to unblock the spades. South's best play will be to take 2 finesses, hoping East has either the ♠Q or the ♥K.",
  "commentary_paragraphs": [
    "There are 11 top tricks (2 spade tricks, the ♥A, 4 diamond tricks, and 4 club tricks). Finessing positions exist in both hearts and spades. By playing for an elimination, South may be able to make the contract even if West has the ♠Q and ♥K.",
    "South should win the club lead and cash 3 more rounds of that suit. The ♦A should be cashed next, followed by a second diamond to the dummy. When diamonds prove to be 3-2 the contract is certain.",
    "South cashes 1 more round of diamonds and leads a heart covering whatever East plays. West can win the trick cheaply, but he will be endplayed. Either a spade or a heart return will provide trick 12 for South.",
    "Notice the importance of keeping a late diamond entry to the dummy. A spade return by West at the time of the endplay will give South a third spade trick, however, the suit will be blocked. Dummy's diamond entry will allow South to untangle the spades.",
    "If West shows out on the second round of diamonds, the endplay will still work as above. If West turns up with 4 diamonds the elimination will no longer work as removing West's exit cards in diamonds will also remove dummy's entry to unblock the spades. South's best play will be to take 2 finesses, hoping East has either the ♠Q or the ♥K."
